        0,
        'The Models API reports each model\'s capabilities, including whether thinking can be disabled, along with its maximum input and output sizes, so code can check support at runtime. A hand-maintained table goes stale, catching a 400 on every call wastes requests and hides the design flaw, and assuming parity is exactly what breaks across releases, as when disabling thinking is accepted on one model and rejected on another.',
