        'High-volume, latency-sensitive, well-defined work such as classification and routing is the case for efficiency-first selection: begin with the fastest, cheapest tier (Haiku 5.5), test on your own data and upgrade only for capability gaps the tests expose. Starting at the top is the capability-first path, suited to complex reasoning and high-stakes accuracy, and at this volume it would burn cost and latency before anything is known. A default tier chosen without measurement is a guess.',
